'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  ch06-logic-declare.spin2
''   Purpose....  Declaring named channels up front, so the LOGIC window
''                labels its own rows
''   Manual.....  P2 Debug Window Manual
''   Version....  v1.1.3 (2026-08-18)
''   Appears in.  Chapter 6: The LOGIC Window - Digital Waveforms --
''                Creating a LOGIC window and declaring channels
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Jul 2026
''   Updated....  Aug 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. Everything below
''   this header is byte-identical to the listing printed there --
''   what you read in the manual is what builds here.
''
'' ===========================================================================

CON _clkfreq = 200_000_000

PUB main() | sample
  ' create + declare 4 channels -- the 1 before each color
  ' is the channel COUNT
  debug(`LOGIC Bus SAMPLES 64 'CLK' 1 $00FF00 'DATA' 1 $FFFF00 'CS' 'WR')

  repeat
    sample := getrnd() & $0F       ' four bits -> the four channels
    debug(`Bus `(sample))          ' feed it by name
    waitms(50)

